\par\par \b \uc2 UnionPay Showcases Innovations with 15 Ecosystem Partners at 2026 China International Financial Exhibition\b0\par\par\uc2 1,068 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 June 2026\par 12:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EQS Newswire / 22/06/2026 / 12:00 CET/CEST \par  \par SHANGHAI, CHINA - Media OutReach Newswire - 22 June 2026 - The 2026 China International Financial Exhibition opened in \par Shanghai on June 16-18. UnionPay, together with 15 global ecosystem partners, showcased its latest achievements in \par global network development, core technological capabilities, open AI ecosystem, consumption growth solutions, and \par ecosystem collaboration. \par Building a Global Payment Network \par Amid a diverse and competitive global payments landscape, UnionPay continues to strengthen its global payment network \par by advancing three strategic pillars: merchant acceptance, local card issuance, and cross-border QR interoperability. \par UnionPay's acceptance network now spans 183 countries and regions, covering over 100 million merchants outside China's \par mainland. UnionPay mobile payment services are available in more than 100 markets, while cards have been rolled out \par across 84 countries and regions outside the Chinese mainland. As of May 2026, transaction volumes generated by \par international cards and wallets in China rose by 54% and 62% respectively year-on-year. A real-time transaction \par dashboard at the exhibition area continuously updated cumulative transaction volumes, highlighting the sustained growth \par of UnionPay's global business. \par Cross-border QR payment interoperability is a centerpiece of UnionPay's international section. The company has \par accelerated partnerships with local payment networks across Southeast Asia, the Middle East, Central Asia, Latin \par America, and Africa to enable QR payment connectivity. On June 11, 2026, the China-Indonesia cross-border QR linkage \par officially went live, witnessed by central bank governors of both countries. The milestone increased the total number \par of overseas merchants accepting UnionPay QR codes to more than 46 million. \par To showcase services catered to inbound visitors, UnionPay has set up a dedicated booth for Nihao China, demonstrating \par the one-stop service app jointly developed with China's Ministry of Culture and Tourism. With over 200,000 registered \par users, the Nihao China app integrates a wide range of travel-related services, including QR payment, public transit, \par voice translation, and tax refunds. The user interface has been fully localized to suit international users. \par UnionPay has been working with global partners to build a cross-border payment ecosystem featuring unified standards, \par orderly development, and shared success. Five international partners have joined UnionPay at this year's exhibition, \par namely, \f28 \uc2 \f2 ASPI\f28 \uc2 \f2  from Indonesia, ZeroPay from South Korea, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dialog Finance\f28 \uc2 \f2  from Sri Lanka, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Halyk Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  from Kazakhstan, and \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco do Brasil\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par Expanding the Ecosystem and Advancing Fintech Innovation \par As digital transformation accelerates, UnionPay remains committed to strengthening independent and secure fintech \par capabilities. The company has been investing in computing infrastructure, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , privacy protection, \par and smart payments. By fostering collaborative innovation among members, universities, technology companies, and \par government agencies, UnionPay expands the ecosystem and supports the development of new productive forces in the \par financial industry. \par The AI exhibition area highlights the progress of UnionPay's National AI Application Pilot Base in the financial \par sector, the only one of its kind in China. UnionPay has established a "1+1+N" large language model architecture \par consisting of an L0 foundation model, an L1 financial payments model, and multiple L2 models specific to different use \par cases. The architecture is supported by a computing resource pool with over 1,000 GPUs and a high-quality 2TB open \par financial dataset. Leveraging a comprehensive payment data infrastructure covering merchants, industry stakeholders, \par users, and use cases, UnionPay delivers robust data support for model training, consumer insights, and intelligent \par decision-making. More than 120 AI applications have been deployed across four key verticals: inclusive finance, \par consumption growth, risk management and compliance, and operational efficiency. To address critical data security \par challenges in the financial sector, UnionPay has pioneered privacy protection technologies for large language model and \par introduced an innovative edge-cloud synergy approach, enabling secure AI services without exposing sensitive data. The \par innovation facilitates broader AI adoption while safeguarding partner data. \par UnionPay's open AI platform brings together the innovative capabilities of ecosystem partners, including banks, payment \par institutions and technology companies. By providing payment, data, and AI-powered services, the platform empowers \par industry participants and fosters collaborative innovation. The exhibition area for smart payments features UnionPay's \par APOP (Agentic Payment Open Protocol), an open framework for agent-based payments. Built on user consent and robust risk \par controls, APOP explores new models for intelligent agents to access payment capabilities. To date, UnionPay has \par partnered with 19 industry players to deploy applications including travel assistants, overseas hotel reservations, \par in-vehicle payments, and utility payments. \par Fudan University, Huawei, Baidu AI Cloud, HYGON, and KUPAS.AI have joined UnionPay as technology partners at the \par exhibition, demonstrating collaborative achievements in computing power, large language models, and cybersecurity. \par Together, they have showcased UnionPay's open innovation ecosystem and its commitment to driving the evolution of the \par payments industry through technological progress. \par Delivering Payment Services that Better Serve Consumers, Businesses, and the Real Economy \par Using Shanghai as a case study, live dashboards at the booth present data insights, including foot traffic heat maps of \par key commercial districts and consumer profiles of domestic and international visitors. Data showed that tourists from \par outside Shanghai account for 55% of total spending in the Nanjing East Road commercial area, making them a key driver \par of consumption. Distinct spending patterns were also observed among inbound travelers: visitors from the US favor local \par street food, South Korean tourists prefer popular lifestyle destinations, and Thai travelers show strong interest in \par shopping. These insights provide valuable support for commercial district operations and cultural tourism promotion. \par At this year's China International Financial Exhibition, UnionPay showcases its extensive global network, solid \par business foundation, and leading technological capabilities through a wide array of immersive exhibits. Moving forward, \par UnionPay will continue to grow its global payment network, develop self-reliant digital and intelligent infrastructure, \par and deliver value to consumers.Hashtag: #UnionPay \par The issuer is solely responsible for the content of this announcement. \par  \par News Source: UnionPay International \par 22/06/2026 Dissemination of a Financial Press Release, transmitted by EQS News. \par The issuer is solely responsible for the content of this announcement. \par Media archive at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.todayir.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.todayir.com}}}\uc2 \f2  \par View original content: EQS News \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Image link: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://track.media-outreach.com/index.php/WebView/472040/225647"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://track.media-outreach.com/index.php/WebView/472040/225647}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Image link: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nwr.eqs-cockpit.com/fncls2.ssx?application_id=2350984&application_name=news&site_id=dow_jones%7e%7e%7ebed8b539-0373-42bd-8d0e-f3efeec9bbed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://nwr.eqs-cockpit.com/fncls2.ssx?application_id=2350984&application_name=news&site_id=dow_jones%7e%7e%7ebed8b539-0373-42bd-8d0e-f3efeec9bbed}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 22, 2026 06:00 ET (10:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260622em6m000m2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
