\par\par \b \uc2 Press Release: \uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2  announces strategic collaboration with \uc2 AWS\uc2  to drive industrial automation and lower-carbon construction globally\b0\par\par\uc2 766 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 June 2026\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 22 June 2026, 08:00 CET\par \par \uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2  today announced a strategic collaboration with \uc2 Amazon Web Services\uc2  (\uc2 AWS\uc2 ) to accelerate industrial automation across its global operations through advanced cloud, \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  and edge technologies.\par \par \uc2 The collaboration brings \uc2 AWS\uc2  cloud and AI capabilities directly to \uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2 's manufacturing processes, providing opportunities for further optimisation and improvement of safety, asset reliability and energy efficiency. \uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2  will converge some of its operational technology (OT) and information technology (IT) on \uc2 AWS\uc2  infrastructure, designed for security and scale, extending cloud and AI to the edge of its production environments. Using \uc2 AWS\uc2  services across industrial IoT, real-time sensor data and machine learning, the company will deploy AI at the point of production, enabling predictive maintenance, computer-vision quality control, process optimisation and digital twins of its physical assets and production lines.\par \par \uc2 Further, to advancing digital and \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  adoption at scale, \uc2 AWS\uc2  will design and deliver a comprehensive education programme for \uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2 's global workforce.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the cloud and AI collaboration, Amazon has entered into a multi-year Supply Framework Agreement with \uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2  for the supply of structural steel across Europe and the United Kingdom. Under this framework, \uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2  will supply lower-carbon XCarb(R) steel for use in Amazon operations facilities and \uc2 AWS\uc2  data centres, supporting Amazon's goal to reach net-zero carbon by 2040. The agreement reflects both companies' shared ambition to advance the decarbonization of building construction at scale.\par \par \uc2 Tanuja Randery, Managing Director and Vice President, EMEA, \uc2 AWS\uc2 , said:\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2  is rethinking how steelmaking works, from predictive maintenance on furnaces and other industrial installations, to AI-driven energy optimisation. By bringing AI to the point of production, they are creating new ways of running safer, more efficient operations across steelmaking sites in 14 countries. We are delighted to work with customers who think at this level, and \uc2 AWS\uc2  is proud to support \uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2 's ambition with cloud, edge, and AI technology built for industrial scale."\par \par \uc2 Nik Puri, Group CIO & CISO at \uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2 , said:\par \par \uc2 "The next frontier of digital transformation for steel is on the plant floor. With \uc2 AWS\uc2 , we are bringing cloud and AI directly to the point of production, connecting our assets and building plants that sense, learn and optimise in real time. By converging our operational and information technology on a single secure platform, we are moving to digitally enabled operations: safer for our people, more reliable in output, and more sustainable by design. This is how we industrialise AI at scale across the steelmaking value chain."\par \par \uc2 ENDS\par \par \uc2 About \uc2 ArcelorMittal\par \par \uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2  is one of the world's leading integrated steel and mining companies with a presence in 60 countries and primary steelmaking operations in 14 countries. It is the largest steel producer in Europe, among the largest in the Americas, and has a growing presence in Asia through its joint venture AM/NS India. \uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2  sells its products to a diverse range of customers including the automotive, engineering, construction and machinery industries, and in 2025 generated revenues of $61.4 billion, produced 55.6 million metric tonnes of crude steel and 48.8 million tonnes of iron ore. Our purpose is to produce smarter steels for people and planet. Steels made using innovative processes which use less energy, emit significantly less carbon and reduce costs. Steels that are cleaner, stronger and reusable. Steels for the renewable energy infrastructure that will support societies as they transform through this century. With steel at our core, our inventive people and an entrepreneurial culture at heart, we will support the world in making that change.\par \par \uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2  is listed on the stock exchanges of New York (MT), Amsterdam (MT), Paris (MT), Luxembourg (MT) and on the Spanish stock exchanges of Barcelona, Bilbao, Madrid and Valencia (MTS). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://corporate.arcelormittal.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://corporate.arcelormittal.com}}}\par \par \uc2 22 Jun 2026 02:00 ET *ArcelorMittal Partners With \uc2 AWS\uc2  to Drive Industrial Automation\par \par \uc2 22 Jun 2026 02:01 ET *\uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2 : To Develop Advanced Cloud, \b \highlight22\uc2 Artificial Intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Edge Technologies\par \par \uc2 22 Jun 2026 02:02 ET *\uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2 : To Use AI at the Point of Production, Enabling Predictive Maintenance\par \par \uc2 22 Jun 2026 02:02 ET *\uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2 : Amazon Has Entered Into a Multi-Year Supply Framework Agreement\par \par \uc2 22 Jun 2026 02:03 ET *\uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2 : Agreement Is for Structural Steel Across Europe, the U.K.\par \par \uc2 22 Jun 2026 02:03 ET *\uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2 : To Supply Lower-Carbon Steel for Facilities, AWS Data Centres\par \par \uc2 22 Jun 2026 02:06 ET *\uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2  Didn't Disclose Financial Details\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 22, 2026 02:06 ET (06:06 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260622em6m000a1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
