\par\par \b \uc2 EQS-News: \uc2 Envision Energy\uc2  Unveils 2026 Net Zero Action Report at VivaTech, Pioneering Future Energy Systems for Civilizational Prosperity\b0\par\par\uc2 928 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 June 2026\par 10:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EQS-News: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Envision Energy\f28 \uc2 \f2  / Key word(s): ESG/Product Launch \par Envision Energy Unveils 2026 Net Zero Action Report at VivaTech, Pioneering Future Energy Systems for Civilizational \par Prosperity \par 2026-06-22 / 10:55 CET/CEST \par The issuer is solely responsible for the content of this announcement. \par  \par =---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \par PARIS, June 22, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Envision Energy\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a global leading green technology company, unveiled its 2026 Net \par Zero Action Report at VivaTech, one of Europe's largest and most influential innovation events. The report highlights \par how the convergence of energy and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is rapidly reshaping industrial systems and even the \par foundations of modern civilization. \par  \par This marks the sixth consecutive year that Envision has published its Net Zero Action Report. This year's edition \par emphasizes that the future of infrastructure will be built on a new-type power system integrating energy, storage, \par grids, computing, and intelligence, forming the backbone of the AI-driven industrial era. \par  \par  \par "A truly transformative energy transition is not merely about replacing old energy sources. It is about creating a new \par generation of civilizational infrastructure that enables sustainable prosperity in the age of AI."\u160\'00\'A0 said Lei Zhang, \par Founder and CEO of Envision,"Energy is not just the foundation of AI - it is the lifeblood of intelligence. As power \par systems becomes the core infrastructure of intelligence era, only by solving full-chain energy management for \par intelligent production can we deliver the abundant, reliable, and sustainable power required for the next industrial \par revolution driven by AI." \par  \par Pioneering AI Power Systems in Practice \par  \par Over the past year, Envision has continued to lead innovation in next-generation power systems, pioneering what it \par defines as AI Power Systems. This integration enables unprecedented efficiency: maximizing the value of every unit of \par green electricity, optimizing computing workloads, and aligning limited power capacity with rapidly growing GPU demand. \par  \par At the Chifeng Net Zero Industrial Park, Envision has already demonstrated this model in operation. Built on a 2 GW, \par 100% renewable power system, the company leverages EnOS and its Energy Foundation Model to orchestrate wind, solar, \par storage, computing workloads and green hydrogen production in real time.In partnership with Tencent, the AI Power \par System is also being used to optimize AI workload scheduling, dynamically matching computing demand with renewable \par energy availability. \par  \par It also lays the foundation for Mission Gobi, Envision's global initiative announced at VivaTech 2026 to develop 5GW of \par green AI data center (AIDC) capacity in desert and arid regions by 2030. \par  \par Envision's Growing Global Footprint and Impact \par  \par The report also highlights how Envision is turning the innovation into real-world impact by supporting energy security, \par industrial transformation and community development. \par  \par In Egypt, Envision's 500MW Amunet Wind Project has entered full operation. As one of Africa's largest wind \par installations in both single-unit scale and total capacity, it generates approximately 2.3 billion kWh annually, enough \par to power around 800,000 households and support Egypt's Vision 2030. \par  \par In the UK, Envision's smart energy storage system powered by the Dubhe Energy Foundation Model is supporting the \par Carrington project, one of the country's largest standalone storage facilities. Once operational, it will supply \par electricity equivalent to 2.2 million households for two hours, while reducing renewable curtailment and enhancing grid \par stability, supporting both energy security and net-zero goals. \par  \par In global green trade, the first shipment of green ammonia produced at Envision's Chifeng Net Zero Industrial Park was \par delivered to \f28 \uc2 \f2 LOTTE Fine Chemical\f28 \uc2 \f2  in South Korea, marking a milestone in the emergence of "green oil" as a global \par zero-carbon commodity. \par  \par  \par At the Monsoon Wind Power Project in Laos, Envision supported the clearance of more than 1,200 landmines and unexploded \par ordnance. In addition to providing clean electricity equivalent to power supply for 1.43 million households in Vietnam \par and creating more than 1,600 local jobs, the project also contributed to local schools through educational support and \par community engagement programs. \par  \par With six consecutive years of publishing its Net Zero Action Report, Envision has evolved from a net-zero pioneer and \par technology partner into a global builder of the infrastructure for a sustainable future. From deserts to demined \par fields, from polar regions to remote islands, the company continues to deploy future energy systems that expand access \par to clean, affordable and reliable power. As AI and clean energy converge, Envision is working to lay the foundations \par for a new era of sustainable prosperity. \par  \par View original content to download multimedia:\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prnewswire.co.uk/news-releases/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.prnewswire.co.uk/news-releases/}}}\uc2 \f2  \par envision-energy-unveils-2026-net-zero-action-report-at-vivatech-pioneering-future-energy-systems-for-civilizational-prosperity-302806207.html \par  \par =---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \par 2026-06-22 CET/CEST Dissemination of a Corporate News, transmitted by EQS News - a service of EQS Group. \par The issuer is solely responsible for the content of this announcement. \par The EQS Distribution Services include Regulatory Announcements, Financial/Corporate News and Press Releases. \par View original content: EQS News \par  \par =---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2350900\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A02026-06-22\u160\'00\'A0CET/CEST\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Image link: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mmx.prnewswire.com/media/MS1869972/668c2236470f4e3783aabe40a27087ff.jpg?id=OA2727163"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://mmx.prnewswire.com/media/MS1869972/668c2236470f4e3783aabe40a27087ff.jpg?id=OA2727163}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Image link: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mmx.prnewswire.com/media/MS1869973/120a08b41a4547149900af3e16c7637d.jpg?id=OA2727164"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://mmx.prnewswire.com/media/MS1869973/120a08b41a4547149900af3e16c7637d.jpg?id=OA2727164}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Image link: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edge.prnewswire.com/c/img/favicon.png?sn=EN88630&sd=2026-06-22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://edge.prnewswire.com/c/img/favicon.png?sn=EN88630&sd=2026-06-22}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Image link: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rt.prnewswire.com/rt.gif?NewsItemId=EN88630&Transmission_Id=202606220449PR_NEWS_EURO_ND__EN88630&DateId=20260622"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://rt.prnewswire.com/rt.gif?NewsItemId=EN88630&Transmission_Id=202606220449PR_NEWS_EURO_ND__EN88630&DateId=20260622}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Image link: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nwr.eqs-cockpit.co