\par\par \b \uc2 Press Release: Press Release: \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  appoints Paulo Fontoura as Global Head of R&D\b0\par\par\uc2 1,492 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 June 2026\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  appoints Paulo Fontoura as Global Head of R&D\par \par \uc2 Paris, June 22, 2026. \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  today announced the appointment of Paulo Fontoura, MD, PhD, FAAN, as Executive Vice President, Global Head of Research & Development Pharma, effective September 1, 2026. He will be a member of \uc2 Sanofi\uc2 's Executive Committee, based in Paris, and will report to Chief Executive Officer \uc2 Bel\u233\'00\'E9n Garijo\uc2 . As head of R&D Pharma, Paulo will lead \uc2 Sanofi\uc2 's end-to-end innovation engine, spanning research, translational medicine, clinical development, and regulatory affairs, with responsibility for advancing a differentiated pipeline and accelerating the delivery of transformative medicines to patients. Paulo succeeds Dr. \uc2 Houman Ashrafian\uc2 , who has decided to pursue an opportunity outside the company.\par \par \uc2 With more than 25 years of experience spanning academic medicine, translational science, clinical development, and pharmaceutical innovation, Paulo joins \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  at an important moment as the company continues to advance its R&D transformation and progress a pipeline of new medicines across multiple therapeutic areas.\par \par \uc2 A board-certified neurologist and physician-scientist, Paulo has played a leading role in the development of significant medicines across neuroscience, immunology, rare diseases, ophthalmology, and infectious diseases. Most recently, he served as Chief Medical Officer of \uc2 Xaira Therapeutics\uc2 , an AI-native biotechnology company focused on transforming drug discovery and development through generative \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Prior to Xaira, he spent more than 15 years at Roche, where he held a series of senior leadership positions culminating as Senior Vice President and Global Head of Clinical Development for Neuroscience, Immunology, Ophthalmology, Infectious and Rare Diseases. During his tenure at Roche, he oversaw a global organization of physicians and clinical scientists and was accountable for managing a broad late-stage portfolio across multiple therapeutic areas. Over the years, his teams contributed to the development of over 60 new molecular entities, across several therapeutic modalities, leading to over 20 \uc2 FDA\uc2  and \uc2 EMA\uc2  first approvals and line extensions, including multiple breakthrough therapies across neuroscience, rare diseases, immunology and ophthalmology.\par \par \uc2 "I want to thank Dr. \uc2 Houman Ashrafian\uc2  for his contribution to our company over the last three years and I wish him all the best in his next chapter. I am delighted to welcome Paulo to the Executive Team. Paulo is a highly respected R&D leader with a strong track record across research, development, and innovation. His scientific expertise, development experience, and leadership of large-scale innovation organizations will be invaluable as we continue to advance our pipeline and shape the future of R&D at \uc2 Sanofi\uc2 ," said \uc2 Bel\u233\'00\'E9n Garijo\uc2 , Chief Executive Officer of \uc2 Sanofi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I am thrilled to join \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  at such an exciting moment," said Paulo Fontoura. "In recent years, \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  has established a leadership position in immunology and built strong positions in several other areas of significant unmet medical need, while demonstrating a clear commitment to scientific innovation and AI-powered transformation. I am deeply honored to join the company at this important moment and help \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  to expand and transform its pipeline and grow its leadership role in biopharma, and I look forward to working with our talented teams to advance breakthrough medicines for patients around the world."\par \par \uc2 Paulo holds an MD and PhD from the \uc2 New University of Lisbon\uc2  and completed postdoctoral training in neuroimmunology at \uc2 Stanford University\uc2 . He is a Fellow of the \uc2 American Academy of Neurology\uc2  and has authored more than 80 peer-reviewed scientific publications.\par \par \uc2 About \uc2 Sanofi\par \par \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  is an R&D driven, AI-powered biopharma company committed to improving people's lives and delivering compelling growth. We apply our deep understanding of the immune system to invent medicines and vaccines that treat and protect millions of people around the world, with an innovative pipeline that could benefit millions more. Our team is guided by one purpose: we chase the miracles of science to improve people's lives; this inspires us to drive progress and deliver positive impact for our people and the communities we serve, by addressing the most urgent healthcare, environmental, and societal challenges of our time. \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  is listed on EURONEXT: SAN and NASDAQ: SNY\par \par \uc2 Media Relations\par \par \uc2 Sandrine Guendoul\uc2  | +33 6 25 09 14 25 | sandrine.guendoul@sanofi.com\par \par \uc2 Evan Berland | +1 215 432 0234 | evan.berland@sanofi.com\par \par \uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9o Le Bourhis | +33 6 75 06 43 81 | leo.lebourhis@sanofi.com\par \par \uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9a Ubaldi | +33 6 30 19 66 46 | lea.ubaldi@sanofi.com\par \par \uc2 Laura Romby| +33 6 74 16 74 29 | laura.romby@sanofi.com\par \par \uc2 Ekaterina Pesheva | +1 410 926 6780 | ekaterina.pescheva@sanofi.com\par \par \uc2 Victor Rouault | +1 617 356 4751 | victor.rouault@sanofi.com\par \par \uc2 Timothy Gilbert | +1 516 521 2929 | timothy.gilbert@sanofi.com\par \par \uc2 Investor Relations\par \par \uc2 Thomas Kudsk Larsen |+ 44 7545 513 693 | thomas.larsen@sanofi.com\par \par \uc2 Aliz\u233\'00\'E9 Kaisserian | + 33 6 47 04 12 11 | alize.kaisserian@sanofi.com